<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C2.S1 — Outcome probability in a rotated basis</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C2.S1 — Born rule on the Bloch sphere</p></div><p>A qubit is prepared in \(|\psi\rangle=\cos(\theta/2)|0\rangle+e^{i\varphi}\sin(\theta/2)|1\rangle\).</p><p>Give the probability of obtaining the outcome \(+1\) when the observable \(X\) is measured, as a simplified function of <code>theta</code> and <code>phi</code>.</p><p>\(p_{+}=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The \(+1\) eigenvector of \(X\) is \(|+\rangle=(|0\rangle+|1\rangle)/\sqrt2\), so</p>\[ p_{+}=|\langle +|\psi\rangle|^{2}=\tfrac12\left|\cos\tfrac\theta2+e^{i\varphi}\sin\tfrac\theta2\right|^{2}. \]<p>Expanding, \(p_+=\tfrac12\big(1+2\cos\tfrac\theta2\sin\tfrac\theta2\cos\varphi\big)=\tfrac12(1+\sin\theta\cos\varphi)\).</p><p>Geometrically this is \(p_\pm=\tfrac12(1\pm\hat n\cdot\vec r)\) with \(\hat n=\hat x\): the probability is an affine function of the projection of the Bloch vector onto the measurement axis.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2024010100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>ta : (1+sin(theta)*cos(phi))/2;</text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="html">
      <text>p+ = (1+sin(theta)cos(phi))/2</text>
    </questionnote>
